.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt CLOWNFILE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm clownfile
.Nd clown per-instance configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Nm
is a TOML file that sets per-directory defaults for a clown session (RFC-0013).
clown assembles the effective configuration by merging several layers, lowest
precedence first, so a higher layer overrides a lower one per key:
.Bl -enum -offset indent
.It
the burned-in default
.Nm
clown ships (the
.Sy [attach]
defaults described below);
.It
the user-global
.Nm
under the XDG config directory \(em
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clown/clownfile ,
or
.Pa ~/.config/clown/clownfile
when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or empty;
.It
every
.Nm
found by ascending from the current directory to
.Ev HOME ,
shallowest first, so a
.Nm
closer to the current directory \(em and
.Pa $HOME/clownfile
itself \(em overrides the XDG file.
.El
An absent
.Nm
at any layer is not an error; a malformed one is.
.Pp
This page documents the
.Sy [profile]
table (run defaults) and the
.Sy [attach]
table (multiplexer self-wrap templates).
.Ss [profile]
The
.Sy [profile]
table provides defaults layered beneath explicit command-line flags and
environment variables.
The named-profile registry
.Pq Fl -profile
is a separate mechanism and wins over these defaults.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy provider
The provider (claude, codex, juggler, opencode, crush).
Applied only when neither
.Fl -provider
nor
.Ev CLOWN_PROVIDER
is set; a clownfile provider also suppresses the interactive profile picker.
.It Sy backend
The tent container backend (podman or lima) used by
.Fl -tent .
.It Sy model
The model.
Injected as
.Fl -model
for the claude-family providers (claude, juggler, clownbox) when the user has not
already passed
.Fl -model ;
other providers source their model elsewhere.
For a
.Fl -profile
named-registry entry
.Pq a separate mechanism from this table's only-if-unset defaults ,
a
.Sy claude Ns -provider
profile with a
.Sy gateway
or
.Sy local
backend and no inline URL instead resolves its model through juggler's
model registry; see
.Xr juggler 7 Sx MODEL REGISTRY .
.It Sy [profile.env]
A table of environment variables exported into the provider and its plugin
servers, set only when not already present (the ambient environment wins).
.It Sy profile
Pins a named registry profile
.Pq Fl -profile
by name.
Unlike the other
.Sy [profile]
keys (only-if-unset defaults), a pin resolves exactly as if
.Fl -profile Ar name
had been passed \(em it suppresses the interactive picker and its
selection is authoritative, not a default.
Resolution order is an explicit
.Fl -profile
flag, then this pin, then clown's burned-in default profile;
an explicit
.Fl -provider
suppresses the pin (and the burned-in default) but never an explicit
.Fl -profile .
.El
.Ss [attach]
The
.Sy [attach]
table is clown's multiplexer/attach layer (RFC-0013 §1.3, RFC-0014).
When
.Sy multiplexer
is set to a value other than
.Ql none ,
clown wraps itself in the configured multiplexer on boot \(em "implicit
per-instance attach" \(em by resolving the configured template and launching the
multiplexer before the provider.
For the interactive
.Sy start
and
.Sy resume
modes clown runs the multiplexer as a child and waits, so it survives the
session and prints the
.Ql clown resume
hint after the multiplexer exits \(em outside it, where the user can catch it.
The placeholder
.Ql {id}
expands to the per-instance session key and the exact element
.Ql {entry}
splices clown's own entrypoint argv;
.Ql {prompt}
and
.Ql {dir}
are available to the spawn templates only.
.Ql {group}
resolves to the group-id and is available in
.Sy resume-title
only (rejected in argv templates).
An unrecognized placeholder is rejected.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy multiplexer
.Ql posh ,
.Ql zmx ,
or
.Ql none .
.Ql none
(and an absent
.Sy [attach] )
runs clown inline.
The burned-in default is
.Ql posh
(the eng-standard portable-shell session manager).
.It Sy group-id
The group key (RFC-0014 §2), env-interpolated at load \(em
.Ql ${NAME}
expands, an unset variable becomes the empty string.
It keys the group chat channel, presence grouping, and the
.Ql {group}
title.
clown exports it as
.Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID ;
empty means ungrouped.
The default binds the orchestrator session key via
.Ql ${SPINCLASS_SESSION_ID} ,
gracefully empty for a bare clown.
.It Sy description
The human-readable presence label (RFC-0014 §4.1), env-interpolated like
.Sy group-id ;
exported as
.Ev CLOWN_GROUP_DESCRIPTION .
.It Sy start
The argv template clown runs for a fresh interactive launch.
.It Sy resume
The argv template clown runs for a reattach (a forwarded
.Fl -resume ,
.Fl r ,
or
.Fl -session-id ,
or
.Nm clown resume ) .
.It Sy resume-title
A string emitted as an OSC-2 terminal title before a resume attach.
.Ql {group}
(the default) resolves to the group-id, falling back to
.Ql {id}
when ungrouped;
.Ql {id}
is also available.
.It Sy spawn
The argv template for a detached-worker launch (RFC-0014 §5), resolved and
executed when an orchestrator passes
.Fl -clown-attach Ns = Ns Ql spawn .
The template must detach (the default uses posh
.Sy attach
with
.Fl -detach )
so clown returns promptly to its launcher.
.It Sy spawn-entry , Sy spawn-window
Parsed and held as schema; not executed by clown this release.
.It Sy pty-suspend
Boolean.
When
.Ql true ,
an interactive provider run is wrapped in clown's escape-to-shell pty proxy:
clown runs the provider on an inner pseudo-terminal and intercepts the escape
key
.Pq Sy escape-key
before the raw-mode TUI swallows it, hands the terminal to
.Sy escape-command ,
and resumes the provider when that command exits.
A raw-mode TUI (such as claude) does not provide this itself.
It is a shell-out, not a job-control suspend, so it works uniformly whether
clown runs inline or as the command inside a multiplexer pane.
Applies to the claude-family providers; it is skipped for
.Fl -tent
(podman manages its own pty) and for exec-replacing providers
.Pq codex , Fl -naked .
Unset is off.
Because it is a boolean with an overridable default, a deeper
.Sy clownfile
may set
.Ql pty-suspend = false
to turn off an enabled default.
.It Sy escape-key
The input key intercepted as the escape trigger, in caret notation
.Pq e.g. Ql ^Z .
Default
.Ql ^Z .
.It Sy escape-command
The argv run, with the terminal handed to it, on the escape key; each element is
env-interpolated
.Pq Ql ${NAME} No / Ql $NAME .
It runs in the worktree
.Pq clown's cwd .
Empty falls back to the user's
.Ev SHELL .
The intended default once spinclass ships
.Ql sc exec
is
.Ql ["sc", "exec", "${SPINCLASS_SESSION_ID}", "$SHELL"] .
.El
.Pp
clown self-execs
.Sy start
and
.Sy resume
only when an interactive terminal is present;
.Ev CLOWN_ATTACH_FORCE Ns = Ns Ql 1
overrides that check for unusual terminals.
Remote (ssh) attach is out of scope and remains spinclass's.
.Pp
clown ships these
.Sy [attach]
defaults burned in as a base clownfile \(em the lowest-precedence layer of the
cascade, merged beneath every discovered
.Sy clownfile .
The burned-in
.Sy multiplexer
defaults to
.Ql posh ,
so clown self-wraps each interactive instance in a posh session unless a
higher-precedence
.Sy clownfile
opts out with
.Sy multiplexer No = Ql none .
The burned-in
.Sy start ,
.Sy resume ,
and
.Sy spawn
templates drive posh
.Sy ( attach No and Sy attach Fl -detach ) .
A discovered
.Sy clownfile
overrides any key.
If the configured multiplexer is not installed, clown runs inline rather than
failing.
The
.Sy spawn ,
.Sy spawn-entry ,
and
.Sy resume-title
defaults equal spinclass's real
.Sy [session-entry]
defaults (FDR-0017 Piece 1);
.Sy start
and
.Sy resume
are clown-native (spinclass had no baked interactive template).
.Ss [messaging]
The
.Sy [messaging]
table opts the session into troupe's XMPP messaging transport (troupe
RFC-0001), so chat reaches sessions on other hosts.
It cascades like the other tables.
clown resolves it and exports the
.Ev TROUPE_TRANSPORT
and
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_*
environment troupe's
.Ic mcp
tools and its per-session
.Ic agent
receiver read.
The default is the local single-host journal; the transport is inert until a
clownfile opts in.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy transport
.Sy local
(default),
.Sy xmpp
(legacy RFC-0001 agent + journal), or
.Sy xmpp-native
(the troupe#3 persistent receiver + minted per-session account).
Anything else is an error.
.It Sy xmpp-domain
The c2s vhost.
.Sy REQUIRED
for both
.Sy xmpp
and
.Sy xmpp-native .
.It Sy xmpp-muc-domain
The base MUC domain rooms are addressed under.
.Sy REQUIRED
for legacy
.Sy transport = "xmpp"
only;
.Sy xmpp-native
addresses rooms by full JID and does not use it.
.It Sy xmpp-host , xmpp-port , xmpp-nick , xmpp-insecure
Optional connection parameters (troupe defaults: DNS-resolve the domain, 5222,
the clown-name, and TLS-verify on).
Emitted only when set.
.It Sy xmpp-user
The authenticated-mode c2s localpart, used only when
.Sy xmpp-password-file
is set (troupe defaults it to the nick).
Omit for the v0 anonymous path.
.It Sy xmpp-password-file
A credential
.Em reference :
a file PATH (environment-interpolated), never the password itself.
clown emits only the path; the secret never enters clown's configuration or a
process environment.
Present only when an authenticated mechanism is used.
.It Sy [[messaging.rooms]]
An array of MUC rooms this session joins under the persistent-receiver model
(clown#213), each a plain room JID plus a per-room wake policy.
clown resolves the set into
.Ev TROUPE_XMPP_ROOMS ,
a comma-separated list of
.Sy jid=policy
pairs (the resolved policy is emitted explicitly).
Empty is valid \(en a session may exchange 1:1 DMs only.
Each entry takes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy jid
The full room JID (environment-interpolated).
.Sy REQUIRED ;
it may not contain a
.Ql \&,
or
.Ql =
(the encoding delimiters).
.It Sy wake
.Sy mentions
(default) \(en wake only on an @-mention of the session's clown-name \(en or
.Sy all
\(en wake on every message in the room.
DMs are native 1:1 and always wake regardless of any room policy.
.El
.El
.Pp
Under
.Sy transport = "xmpp-native"
with a minted credential, clown also registers a session output tee
(troupe#21): a
.Sy Stop
hook that, at the end of each turn, posts the turn's user-visible assistant
reply text verbatim into the session's per-worktree MUC channel
.Pq Ql <repo>.<worktree>@<rooms-domain> ,
derived from the session identity exactly as troupe's derived-rooms join
(troupe#24), via
.Ic troupe muc send .
The post goes out under the session's own nick, so the receiver's self-echo
suppression keeps the tee from waking the session that produced it.
It is best-effort and detached: a failure or an unreachable server drops the
post rather than disturbing the session.
.Pp
When
.Sy transport = "xmpp"
and a required coordinate is missing, clown errors at launch
.Pq the config layer ,
rather than letting the failure surface opaquely inside the troupe child.
.Ss [providers]
.Sy [providers]
holds cross-provider launch policy that is not specific to one backend.
It cascades like the tables above.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy hermetic-config
Boolean, default
.Sy true .
Makes clown's generated provider configuration authoritative for the
config-file providers
.Pq Sy opencode , Sy crush
by suppressing or outranking repository-local configuration files.
.Pp
Without it, a repository-local
.Pa opencode.json
replaces a same-named entry in the
.Sy mcp
map clown generates, so any repository clown is run in can silently repoint a
clown-managed MCP server at a URL of its choosing.
For
.Sy opencode
clown sets
.Ev OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG ;
for
.Sy crush ,
which has no equivalent switch, clown writes its configuration into the
workspace slot at
.Pa <data-dir>/crush.json
and passes
.Fl -data-dir ,
that slot being last in crush's merge order.
.Pp
The user's own global configuration is unaffected in both cases: only the
per-repository file is suppressed, since that is the one an untrusted
repository controls.
Set to
.Sy false
to restore the previous merge behavior.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/clown/crush/ Ns Aq hash
clown's per-project
.Sy crush
data directory, holding crush's workspace configuration and its sessions.
Keyed by a hash of the project path, and stable across launches so
.Cm crush --continue
keeps working.
Created only when
.Sy hermetic-config
is enabled.
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clown/clownfile
The user-global
.Nm ,
falling back to
.Pa ~/.config/clown/clownfile
when
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or empty.
Sits above the burned-in default but below the
.Ev HOME Ns -to-current-directory
ascent, so any
.Pa clownfile
in that ascent overrides it.
This is the recommended location for a personal
.Nm
and is what clown's home-manager module writes by default.
.It Pa $HOME/clownfile
The top of the ascent; a user-global
.Nm
that overrides the XDG file.
Still supported for back-compat, but
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clown/clownfile
is preferred.
.It Pa ./clownfile
A directory-local
.Nm ,
the highest precedence in the cascade.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[profile]
provider = "claude"
model = "claude-sonnet-4-6"

[profile.env]
ANTHROPIC_LOG = "info"

[attach]
multiplexer = "posh"
group-id = "${SPINCLASS_SESSION_ID}"
description = "${SPINCLASS_DESCRIPTION}"
start = ["posh", "attach", "{id}", "{entry}"]
resume = ["posh", "attach", "{id}", "{entry}"]
resume-title = "{group}"
spawn = ["posh", "attach", "{id}", "--detach", "{entry}"]
spawn-entry = ["clown", "--", "{prompt}"]
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown-presence 1 ,
.Xr ringmaster 1 ,
.Xr troupe 1 ,
.Xr juggler 7
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC-0013 (clownfile, per-instance identity, and clown-owned chat);
RFC-0014 (clown-spinclass awareness seam: group-id and presence).
